===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To cause [[annoyance]] or [[distress]] to.
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} To [[discourage]]; to [[deject]].
#*{{RQ:Shakespeare Julius Caesar|V|iii|passage=His funeral shall not be in our camp, / Lest it '''discomfort''' us.}}

====Usage notes====
As a verb, the unrelated term {{m|en|discomfit}} is often used instead, largely interchangeably, though this is proscribed by some as an error, {{m|en||discomfit}} originally meaning “destroy”, not “distress”.

